<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?>
<!DOCTYPE plist PUBLIC "-//Apple//DTD PLIST 1.0//EN" "http://www.apple.com/DTDs/PropertyList-1.0.dtd">
<!--
  com.kotoba.innen-tick.plist  |  the residency for the 因縁 record.

  WARNING: never write two consecutive hyphens inside an XML comment. XML
  forbids them, and a malformed plist does NOT fail loudly: launchd simply
  declines to load it, which is the least visible way for a residency to be
  absent. Refer to ProgramArguments below rather than naming flags here.
  (The sibling observatory plist carries the same warning because its first
  version was broken exactly this way.)

  Why this file exists at all: scripts/tick.cljs said it was "registered with
  tamaki and run by launchd". Measured 2026-08-22, both halves were false.
  tamaki listed loop-innen only as an example line in its README, and no
  launchd job for this loop existed on the operator machine while a dozen
  sibling residencies were loaded. The record stopped growing on 2026-08-12
  and nothing reported that it had.

  Why launchd: this workspace already put its periodic work there
  (com.gftd.fleet-ci-tip-tick, com.gftd.observatory-run, com.gftd.hirameki-harvest).
  A second scheduler splits the answer to "what is running here" in two.

  Why through tamaki: tamaki exec wraps the whole tick as ONE AgentRun, so
  tamaki status shows one run per tick with its real exit code, while this
  repo's ledger/loop-innen-ledger.edn keeps the per cycle detail. Two records,
  each authoritative for its own thing. Verified 2026-08-22 that tamaki exec
  runs the command with cwd set to the project.

  Why every six hours at :47 past: the tick skips publication when nothing
  changed, so an idle cycle is cheap, but Wikidata does not move fast enough
  to reward hourly polling. Minute 47 is unused; the nearest neighbours are
  kouhou-ingest at 6:41 and hirameki-harvest at :37, both different workloads.

  Install:
    cp scripts/com.kotoba.innen-tick.plist ~/Library/LaunchAgents/
    plutil -lint ~/Library/LaunchAgents/com.kotoba.innen-tick.plist
    launchctl bootstrap gui/$(id -u) ~/Library/LaunchAgents/com.kotoba.innen-tick.plist
    launchctl kickstart -p gui/$(id -u)/com.kotoba.innen-tick
  Stop:
    launchctl bootout gui/$(id -u)/com.kotoba.innen-tick

  This job COMMITS AND PUSHES to loop-innen main when the record grows. That is
  the point of a residency, and it is also why the log paths below matter: read
  /tmp/innen-tick.err before believing a quiet week.
-->
<plist version="1.0">
<dict>
  <key>Label</key>
  <string>com.kotoba.innen-tick</string>
  <key>ProgramArguments</key>
  <array>
    <string>/bin/zsh</string>
    <string>-lc</string>
    <string>cd /Users/junkawasaki/github/com-junkawasaki/orgs/etzhayyim/tamaki &amp;&amp; exec ./bin/tamaki exec "innen record tick" --project /Users/junkawasaki/github/com-junkawasaki/orgs/kotoba-lang/loop-innen -- nbb --classpath "../innen/src:src:scripts" scripts/tick.cljs --root /Users/junkawasaki/github/com-junkawasaki --depth 2</string>
  </array>
  <key>RunAtLoad</key>
  <false/>
  <key>StartCalendarInterval</key>
  <array>
    <dict><key>Hour</key><integer>2</integer><key>Minute</key><integer>47</integer></dict>
    <dict><key>Hour</key><integer>8</integer><key>Minute</key><integer>47</integer></dict>
    <dict><key>Hour</key><integer>14</integer><key>Minute</key><integer>47</integer></dict>
    <dict><key>Hour</key><integer>20</integer><key>Minute</key><integer>47</integer></dict>
  </array>
  <key>StandardOutPath</key>
  <string>/tmp/innen-tick.log</string>
  <key>StandardErrorPath</key>
  <string>/tmp/innen-tick.err</string>
</dict>
</plist>
